    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43199" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scythŏpŏlis</span></b> ,
			is, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκυθόπολις,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of
			Palestine</i>, now <i>Bysān</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 18,
				16, § 74</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2
				Macc. 12, 29</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scythŏpŏlītae</span></b> ,
				ārum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Scythopolis</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2
				Macc. 12, 30</span></i>.</div>
